      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Apologies for the confusion. In APA 7th edition, you do sometimes use \"et al.\" shortly after the citation's first use. For references with five or more authors, you include only the first author's name followed by \"et al.\" from that first citation onward. For Chicago author order, if the source has five or more authors, you list up to the fifth author upon first citation and then use \"et al.\" for subsequent citations similar to APA, with the \"et al.\" for authors beginning from the sixth citation onward. I appreciate you pointing these out, and I’ll ensure to give you the corrected information.",
